1. Nc3 e5 (1... d5 {leads to Albin's counter-gambit, played by W with a move
in hand:} 2. d4 e5 ({this could be dodged by} 2... e6) ({or} 2... Bf5 {but the
latter needs a good deal of management})) 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 (
4... d5 {was better.}) 5. Bg5 Be7 (5... Bb4 {was Black's last chance; after
Be7 he is lost.}) 6. Nf5 Nh5 (6... O-O 7. Nxe7+ Nxe7 8. Bxf6 {wins no doubt
eventually.}) 7. Nxe7 Nxe7 8. e4 Nf6 9. e5 Nfg8 10. Bc4 {Of the two decisive
attacks (10 Nd5 and 10 Bc4) W chooses the less obvious and more effective. He
threatened to win the KR.} d6 11. Qh5 g6 12. Qf3 Be6 13. Bxe6 fxe6 14. O-O-O d5
15. Ne4 (15. Nxd5 {also wins; but is no better than the move actually made.})
15... Kd7 16. Nc5+ Kc8 17. Bf6 Nxf6 18. Qxf6 {Sources: Hastings and St
Leonards Observer, 31 December 1921 (Brian Denman Collection)} 1-0

