1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. d3 d6 5. Be3 {The score gives 5 'B KB'.} Bg4
6. Be2 Bxf3 7. Bxf3 Qd7 8. h3 Be7 9. a3 Rd8 10. Qd2 Nd4 11. Bxd4 exd4 12. Nd5
Nxd5 13. exd5 O-O 14. g4 {The score just gives 14 'P Kt4'.} Rfe8 {'The score
gives 14...'KP K1'.} 15. O-O-O h6 16. h4 Qb5 {The score gives 16...'A Kt4'. It
has been assumed that the symbol 'A' stands for queen. 'A' is also given for
White's 18th move.} 17. Rh3 f6 18. Qf4 c6 19. Qf5 cxd5 20. g5 fxg5 21. Bxd5+
Kh8 22. Rg1 Qd7 23. Be6 {The score gives 23 'B Kt'.} Qc6 24. hxg5 {It has
proved very difficult to interpret the score of this game. Source: Bexhill
Chronicle, Visitors' List & East Sussex Guardian, 31 December 1921 (Brian
Denman Collection) Ella Margaret Beddall (1892-1968) married the chess writer
Brian Harley (1883-1955) in 1926.} 1-0

